    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on high-efficiency, top-of-the-order hitters facing favorable matchups. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) anchors our outfield, benefiting from a massive +14% park factor boost and an ideal platoon matchup against Lugo. Joining him at the top of the production charts are **James Wood** (75.37) and **Brice Turang** (75.06), both of whom capitalize on excellent batting order placement and advantageous SP skill ratings. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) rounds out our elite tier, as a +10% park factor and +8% SP skill adjustment propel him past his base projection, making him a critical start against Montero.\n\nThe decision to bench **Austin Riley** (46.04) was the most difficult of the day, as he narrowly missed the cut behind **Josh Naylor** (55.42) and **Isaac Paredes** (60.80). While **Austin Riley** provided a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Isaac Paredes**, who commands a +9% boost from the platoon advantage against Rocker. We are closely monitoring the status of **Dalton Rushing** (41.25), as his score assumes a #9 lineup spot; should he be shifted higher in the order, his utility as a catcher with slow-delivery-dependent SB potential increases. Conversely, we are mitigating risk with **Corbin Carroll** (58.33) and **Seiya Suzuki** (47.68), both of whom face high-skill arms and wind-in conditions that dampen their raw output. **Jose Caballero** remains a marginal start, as a severe -9% wind penalty and a tough matchup against a team that suppresses stolen bases force us to temper expectations for his total contribution.",
